      "pageTitle": "Nick Wright offers $1 million bet to expose Clay Travis",
      "pageDescription": "Nick Wright recently exposed Clay Travis for fabricating political beliefs to arouse his following, and he’s willing to bet $1 million on it.",
      "evidenceText": "Nick Wright offers $1 million bet to expose Clay Travis Skip to content Credit: FS1, Sport & State By Brandon Contes on 11/12/2026 11/12/2026 Less AI and more AA in your search results. Nick Wright recently exposed Clay Travis for fabricating political beliefs to arouse his following, and he’s willing to bet $1 million on it. Wright joined Tim Miller on The Bulwark Daily podcast this week, where the FS1 host pulled back the curtain to reveal that Travis once admitted his beliefs and opinions are crafted for audience enrichment . According to Wright, Travis made the admission at a dinner about 11 years ago. Believing that’s worse than just having different political opinions, Wright told Travis he could not respect him, and claims to have left the dinner. Predictably, Travis fired back Wednesday night, attempting to dispute Wright by saying, “I guess this is what happens when you start voting Republican, people make up entire stories about you in their heads and share it with their far left wing friends.” Thursday morning, Wright had one final response to Travis, giving a detailed recount of the interaction 11 years ago and noting he has witnesses who will defend his side of the story before offering to bet $1 million to prove he’s telling the truth. I’m not going to go back and forth with you (it’s football season for God’s sake!), but I can’t believe you’re actually denying this interaction so I’ll jog your memory: August of 2016, during the Olympics, at the (now shuttered) Intercontinental hotel, a couple blocks from the Fox lot off Pico. We had just finished a night show that no longer exists where (among other things) we debated the Summer Olympics (it was a bad segment because we didn’t have rights to the footage, so we could only show still pictures of what we were talking about) & went to have a drink/meal with a colleague who was on the show with us. The exchange I discussed happened in the lobby bar, at a table with said colleague, and then after I said what I needed to say to to you I went outside and bummed a cigarette off a valet. We haven’t spoken in person since. You know as well as I do this is 100% true, and verifiable, by the colleague that was with us and/or our then bosses who contemporaneously heard the story. We actually also had the same agent at the time, and you and I both know he heard the story and could confirm it as well. So, I’ll pull a page out of your book; I’ll bet you $1,000,000 I’m telling the truth. I assume you’ll pretend you never saw this tweet & continue the grift. And that’s cool, but we both know what the facts are. Also, let this be a reminder that while you have found an amazing lane where you often are actually the smartest guy in the room, this ain’t that lane. So my advice would be to tread carefully. — nick wright (@getnickwright) November 12, 2026 “I’ll pull a page out of your book; I’ll bet you $1,000,000 I’m telling the truth,” Wright wrote. “Also, let this be a reminder that while you have found an amazing lane where you often are actually the smartest guy in the room, this ain’t that lane. So my advice would be to tread carefully.” Travis responded again by attempting to claim Wright just has a personal issue with him over Black Lives Matter. But in his response, which was surely meant to dunk on Wright, Travis claimed COVID broke him, leading him to vote for a Republican president for the first time in 2020. Travis then went on to say he would be willing to bet $1 million with Wright if a lie detector is involved so they can discuss transgender athletes, which has absolutely nothing to do with the bet Wright offered first. I can’t respond to @getnickwright’s post to me because he’s had me blocked on here since I said BLM was a total fraud and that LeBron faked the “hate crime” at his LA mansion. I was right, of course, about both of these things. I was a Democrat in 2015 — and 2016 — which he now says is the date of our dinner. He did not storm out of a dinner after telling me off. This is a very girly thing to brag about, but I’m pretty sure I would remember that because I would have found it funny. I don’t recall our dinner conversation from a decade ago, but I would presume it was similar to this private email I sent Nick that he posted on here back in 2017. You can read that if you wish. At the time I considered myself a radical moderate and felt alienated from the far left and far right. https://t.co/MKZnxUKEko Nick seems to spend a lot of time thinking about me since he’s now posted private emails and talked about private dinners from a decade+ ago. I’m flattered to be so memorable to him. I didn’t vote for a Republican for president until 2020. Covid radicalized me, as it did many people. As I’ve said and written for years, I didn’t leave the Democrat party, the Democrat party left me. If Nick wants to bet a million dollars on do I believe the things I say, I guess we can get a lie detector machine and fire it up. The first question can be, do you believe men pretending to be women should be allowed to play in women’s sports? I’m petty confident I will pass the test when I say hell no. Will you pass when you say yes, Nick? — Clay Travis (@ClayTravis) November 12, 2026 The bet Wright proposed was that his recall of Travis admitting he crafts political opinions for engagement 11 years ago was correct, and that Travis is now lying by claiming the conversation never happened. In the wake of their social media interaction, Wright has received strong support, with others sharing their own stories about when they learned Travis was a political grifter. the late, great ed aschoff told me a similar story in 2018. about how they were once cool but that he couldn’t fuck with travis after he revealed it was all an act. — Joel D. Anderson 🆓 (@byjoelanderson) November 12, 2026 I’m honestly surprised that people are surprised by this. It’s one of the worst kept secrets in our business that dude has been lying about his political beliefs for a long time. I also have some receipts, but I’ll keep those to myself. Make no mistake, he isn’t the only one. There’s a lot of people in our business who are cosplaying for clicks and views. It’s one of the most shameful and dishonest things that one can do. I applaud Nick for keep it real. — Jemele Hill (@jemelehill) November 12, 2026 An old clip of Pardon My Take’s PFT Commenter claiming Travis once admitted to him that he saw an open market for a right-leaning sports host also resurfaced. PFT has the same basic story as @getnickwright: “Clay’s such a fraud. He literally told me back in like 2015, ‘There’s no market out there right now for right wing sports, so I’m just going to start becoming a right wing sports [guy]’ – he told me what he was going to do.” https://t.co/eAUR8xRkJ5 — Elijah Cone (@ElijahCone) November 12, 2026 Interestingly, PFT said the interaction with Travis occurred in 2015, which aligns with the 11-year-old conversation Wright recalls having with the Sport & State founder. While Travis says COVID “radicalized me,” he previously described the 2015 protests at the University of Missouri as his “ red pill, ” which again matches the timing of the conversations he allegedly had with PFT and Wright. Travis has been open about previously identifying as a Democrat. He’s been open about not voting for Trump in 2016, and only voting for his first Republican presidential candidate in 2020. He’s been open about seeing an available market for right-leaning sports content. Everyone knows his background is not that of a lifelong conservative. So, what part of Wright’s story is Travis really contesting? About Brandon Contes Brandon Contes is a staff writer for Awful Announcing and The Comeback. He previously helped carve the sports vertical for Mediaite and spent more than three years with Barrett Sports Media. Send tips/comments/complaints to bcontes@thecomeback.com View all posts by Brandon Contes Follow on Twitter Related Content Corned beef, Cheerwine, and carving stations: Ranking every NHL team’s media meals Where have you gone, Lee Corso? College football fans falling out of love with Saturday pregame shows Five players who deserved to win the Heisman Trophy but didn’t Why Joe Buck and Troy Aikman is the most painful breakup in sports media history Recent Posts Washington Commanders quarterback Sam Hartman will follow in the footsteps of Jesse Palmer in starring as 'The Bachelor.' Brett Yormark is leaving the Big 12 to run a new venture for Redbird Capital built around their ownership of AC Milan. The NHL is ready to come to the negotiating table to renew its rights with ESPN and TNT at an increase over its current deal. Credit: ‘Run It Back’ on FanDuel TV \"You gotta be kidding me!\" 'When We Were Young and Fearless' examines how Kevin Durant, Russell Westbrook, and James Harden changed the NBA. Sidebar Popular Posts The 76ers are either building a superteam or creating a superproblem Is a sports media blue wave coming, too? Recent Posts Washington Commanders quarterback Sam Hartman will follow in the footsteps of Jesse Palmer in starring as 'The Bachelor.' Brett Yormark is leaving the Big 12 to run a new venture for Redbird Capital built around their ownership of AC Milan. The NHL is ready to come to the negotiating table to renew its rights with ESPN and TNT at an increase over its current deal. Credit: ‘Run It Back’ on FanDuel TV \"You gotta be kidding me!\" 'When We Were Young and Fearless' examines how Kevin Durant, Russell Westbrook, and James Harden changed the NBA.",
