      "evidenceText": "Student Press Report – CollegeJournalism.org Student Press Report The Student Press Report is a national news desk covering student media and journalism education in higher ed. It is supported by lead partners  Student Press Law Center  and  Flytedesk , with secondary support from the  Associated Collegiate Press , the  Association of University Student Media Managers , the  College Media Business and Advertising Managers  and  CollegeJournalism.org . Learn more about republishing, editorial independence, pitch guidelines and the AI ethics policy. Latest stories Meet the college editors teaching journalism to high schoolers At the Nashville SUNN, teenagers learn it all, from story pitches to publication For student newsrooms, the midterms present a steep but important learning curve College journalists are embracing their responsibility to educate and inform campus and community about elections — many for the first time The open records stonewalling is working As a student journalist, I get exhausted managing my course load, a newspaper and the records custodians determined to deny us College journalism is thriving at schools that don’t teach it Hundreds of college newspapers publish at universities that don’t offer journalism majors — and that’s no problem for the students. A ‘reason to be optimistic about the future of journalism’ Connecticut Mirror’s Student Voices program provides the training and platform for young opinion writers — 300-plus and counting Like Millennials with social media, will news execs force Gen Z to set the AI agenda? Out of fear and confusion, we handed the social media leadership keys to early-career journalists. Let’s take a more collaborative approach with AI. Philanthropy must invest in student journalists Giving to young journalists pays off over decades — not overnight The reporting their universities didn’t want Four college journalists speak out on the importance of standing up to administrators The next gene