      "pageDescription": "When Poynter launched our AI guidelines in 2024, the product was the result of listening to newsrooms, editors and reporters who shared their insight and expertise on how AI was impacting them. As the technology shifted and your work changed rapidly with it, we continued to update our guidelines. We learned that AI guidance cannot be static, and we need to hear directly and regularly from as wide a range of journalism professionals as possible in order to provide current and useful AI resources. Your insights are critical to this work.\nAs we approach 2027, we are asking for your input to help us update and revise our AI policy guidance. Please be part of the process by completing this short (~10 minute) survey to help us understand where and how newsrooms are using AI. Your confidential re",
      "evidenceText": "Poynter newsroom AI survey Poynter newsroom AI survey When Poynter launched our AI guidelines in 2024, the product was the result of listening to newsrooms, editors and reporters who shared their insight and expertise on how AI was impacting them. As the technology shifted and your work changed rapidly with it, we continued to update our guidelines. We learned that AI guidance cannot be static, and we need to hear directly and regularly from as wide a range of journalism professionals as possible in order to provide current and useful AI resources. Your insights are critical to this work. As we approach 2027, we are asking for your input to help us update and revise our AI policy guidance. Please be part of the process by completing this short (~10 minute) survey to help us understand where and how newsrooms are using AI. Your confidential response will be used to help guide and form our policy updates. Sign in to Google to save your progress. Learn more * Indicates required question About you Newsroom name * Your answer Your role/job title * Your answer Newsroom size * 1 2-5 6-15 16-50 50+ staff Next Page 1 of 8 Clear form Never submit passwords through Google Forms. This form was created inside of Poynter. Does this form look suspicious? Report   Forms       Help and feedback       Contact form owner       Help Forms improve       Report",
